@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> ACQUIRING_START

ACQUIRING_START --> TOP : stable top/start posture acquired\ntracking valid for dwell window
TOP --> ECCENTRIC : sustained elbow flexion trend\n+ body-local wrist descent/toward-torso trend
ECCENTRIC --> BOTTOM : sufficient descent/ROM evidence\n+ local minimum / velocity reversal evidence
BOTTOM --> CONCENTRIC : sustained elbow extension trend\n+ body-local wrist ascent/away-from-torso trend
CONCENTRIC --> REP_COMPLETE : TOP reacquired\n+ minimum ROM satisfied\n+ minimum rep duration satisfied
REP_COMPLETE --> TOP : increment rep count once\nstart next-cycle observation

ECCENTRIC --> TOP : early reversal before valid bottom\nABORTED/PARTIAL; no rep count
CONCENTRIC --> ACQUIRING_START : sustained reversal/failure before top\nFAILED/PARTIAL; no rep count
BOTTOM --> ACQUIRING_START : movement becomes indeterminate\nbefore valid concentric phase

TOP --> ACQUIRING_START : material setup/view change
ECCENTRIC --> ACQUIRING_START : TemporalResetCoordinator reset
BOTTOM --> ACQUIRING_START : TemporalResetCoordinator reset
CONCENTRIC --> ACQUIRING_START : TemporalResetCoordinator reset
REP_COMPLETE --> ACQUIRING_START : TemporalResetCoordinator reset

note right of ACQUIRING_START
Do not infer a rep phase immediately after tracking recovery or setup change.
Acquire a fresh stable movement state before counting again.
end note

note right of TOP
TOP is exercise-specific and configuration-aware.
Do not define it with one universal elbow-angle magic number.
Use calibrated/configured evidence plus stability/hysteresis.
end note

note right of ECCENTRIC
Primary evidence combines trends rather than one coordinate:
- elbow flexion trend,
- body-local wrist trajectory,
- velocity direction,
- confidence-qualified landmarks.
end note

note right of BOTTOM
BOTTOM is supported by local movement evidence such as a sufficiently deep
descent and direction/velocity reversal, with hysteresis and minimum dwell.
Thresholds belong in rule/analyzer config and tests.
end note

note right of CONCENTRIC
A grinder may remain CONCENTRIC while velocity is low if direction remains
consistent and tracking is valid. Do not fail a rep merely because it is slow.
end note

note right of REP_COMPLETE
Count exactly once only after a valid full sequence reaches a stable TOP
with minimum ROM and duration satisfied. RepFinalizationBundle is then emitted.
end note

note bottom
Any significant tracking gap, material camera/view transform change,
exercise/setup parameter change, or explicit TemporalResetCoordinator event
invalidates the current temporal rep state and returns to ACQUIRING_START.
The interrupted rep is never resumed across the discontinuity.
end note

@enduml
